U6TGFiZWwzMTY2MTI2ODA3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/labels/S-Needs-Investigation","name":"S-Needs-Investigation","color":"D876E1","default":false,"description":"This issue requires detective work to figure out what's going wrong"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-09-12T17:50:16Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T23:50:11Z","closed_at":"2025-12-09T23:50:11Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bevy version and features\n\n- Bevy 16.1, default features\n\n## What you did\n\nI have a custom asset loader that immediately loads another asset on which it depends. The loader for the immediately loaded asset also starts loading an image and stores that handle in the asset, but the image never starts loading.\n\nMinimal repro: https://github.com/mxjp/bevy-nested-asset-loader-bug-repro\n\n## What went wrong\n\nI would expect that assets loaded via `load_context::load` always start loading at some point, even if loading of the current asset is done via `load_context::loader().immediate().load`.\n\n## Additional information\n\nA possible workaround is to manually load the image a second time via the asset server which also fixes the previously broken asset handle. The repo mentioned above includes two places where this can be done to prove, that everything else works.\n\nUsing `load_context::load` in the inner asset loader with a path that doens't exist never produces any kind of error message.\n","closed_by":{"login":"alice-i-cecile","id":3579909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Nzk5MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3579909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile","html_url":"https://github.com/alice-i-cecile","followers_url":"ht